	•	Fast dynamic response: No rotor current lag (unlike induction motors), leading to better control precision.
	•	High starting torque: Even at zero speed when paired with advanced control strategies such as FOC or DTC.

3.3 Thermal Management and Reliability

MOSFETs such as IRF1407 with low Rds(on) and high current capacity (up to 130A) are used in the inverter stage. Combined with heatsinks and proper PCB design, the motor drive remains reliable under peak load conditions. PWM modulation and dead-time control enhance the robustness of the switching stage.

3.4 Cost-Efficiency and Integration

Compared to IPM motors, SPM motors offer lower cost and easier integration with standard motor controllers. They are widely used in entry-level and consumer-grade applications, as well as in academic settings for control system prototyping.




