Full-Bridge Inverter Configuration

The second and most widely adopted configuration is the full-bridge inverter (shown in Figure 3.3). In this configuration, each motor phase is controlled by two complementary switches (upper and lower), totaling six power switches. This setup can accommodate both Y-connection and delta-connection motor windings.

