Sensor vs. Sensorless Trapezoidal Control

In trapezoidal control, the feedback signal can either come from:
	•	A position sensor (sensor-based), or
	•	Be inferred from back-EMF (sensorless).

Sensorless disadvantage:
	•	No back-EMF is generated at standstill; hence the motor cannot start directly from zero speed.

Solution:
	•	A predefined startup sequence is used to apply controlled current pulses, forcing the rotor to move slightly.
	•	Once movement generates sufficient back-EMF, normal sensorless operation resumes.

